es/45070"} "Suzie Landells"] " who had barely qualified for the final, placing eighth by 1/100th of a second. In 1986 Landells won both IMs at the Commonwealth Games. Another surprise in Los Angeles was the bronze medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/47766"} "Petra Zindler"] " of West Germany. Her best time in 1984 was only 4:52.38, but she qualified third fastest and matched that in the final, improving to 4:48.57."] "\n\n" [:p {} "At the Friendship Games, three weeks hence, this event was won by Soviet swimmer " [:a {:href "/athletes/50682"} "Yelena Dendeberova"] " in 4:43.78, well off Caulkins’ Olympic winning time, and trailed by East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/47510"} "Kathleen Nord"] ", who Caulkins considered her biggest rival in 1984, but who swam poorly to finish in 4:49.49."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "243"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50983"} "Tracy Caulkins"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "4:44.42 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "4:39.24 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45070"} "Suzie Landells"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "4:54.13 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "4:48.30 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "105"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47766"} "Petra Zindler"]] [:td {} 